def flatten(xs):
    """Flatten nested lists of integers iteratively, preserving order."""
    flat = []
    stack = [iter(xs)]
    while stack:
        try:
            item = next(stack[-1])
        except StopIteration:
            stack.pop()
        else:
            if isinstance(item, list):
                stack.append(iter(item))
            else:
                flat.append(item)
    return flat

This is iterative and preserves order. Example:
